From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wize-logic <wizelogic@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:11:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] recomp: short rep movs, stos and cmps inline

MSVC's memcpy is `rep movsd` for the dwords and `rep movsb` for the 0..3
bytes left, so every copy lifted to two memcpy calls with their range
checks, the second of 0..3 bytes, and a copy or fill of a few dwords paid
for the call too (in Halo, about 500 such calls a frame).

rep movs and rep stos now move or store up to 3 elements in the element
loop, one by one as the hardware does (each a guest access, so an MMIO
window and an overlapping copy see what they saw), with no call;
only longer or backward runs reach the general form. The instruction
before one in its block says more: after `and ecx, n` (n <= 3) the
general form is left out, after `mov ecx, n` (n <= 4) the
elements are moved with no test at all. A rep compare after `mov ecx, n`
(n <= 4; a GUID is `mov ecx, 4; repe cmpsd`) is unrolled forwards.

Two fixes on the way: rep stosb's memset ran over whatever edi pointed
at, MMIO and a range wrapping the address space included (now checked
as rep stosd and rep movs check it), and a rep compare that computes CF
read each element twice (two volatile reads of a device register).
